<div class="custom-tables-settings-body">

    <div class="config-card">
        <h3><i class="fas fa-dice-d20"></i> Custom Tables</h3>

        <p class="dqa-ct-hint">
            Drag roll tables here from the Rollable Tables directory or from a compendium. They
            will be listed by <strong>QuickActions.CustomTables()</strong>.
        </p>

        <div class="dqa-drop-zone">
            <i class="fas fa-dice-d20"></i>
            <span>Drop a Rollable Table here</span>
        </div>

        <ol class="dqa-table-list">
            {{#each tables}}
            <li class="dqa-table-row {{#if this.missing}}dqa-missing{{/if}}">
                <div class="dqa-table-info">
                    <span class="dqa-table-name">{{this.label}}</span>
                    <span class="dqa-table-source">
                        {{#if this.missing}}Not found — the table was deleted or its compendium is unavailable{{else}}{{this.results}} entries{{/if}}
                    </span>
                </div>
                <button type="button" class="dqa-icon-btn" data-action="removeTable" data-uuid="{{this.uuid}}"
                        data-tooltip="Remove" aria-label="Remove {{this.label}}">
                    <i class="fas fa-trash"></i>
                </button>
            </li>
            {{/each}}

            {{#unless hasTables}}
            <li class="dqa-empty">No tables configured yet.</li>
            {{/unless}}
        </ol>

        <button type="button" class="reset-btn" data-action="clearTables" {{#unless hasTables}}disabled{{/unless}}>
            <i class="fas fa-trash"></i> Clear All
        </button>
    </div>

    <div class="config-card">
        <h3><i class="fas fa-circle-info"></i> Before You Start</h3>

        <p class="field-hint">
            <strong>Players need to see the table.</strong> A roll table created in the sidebar
            starts with no player access at all, so it works for you and fails for them. Set its
            ownership to <em>Observer</em> — and do the same for the compendium holding the items
            it hands out, which is one setting for the whole pack.
        </p>
        <p class="field-hint">
            <strong>Items only.</strong> Results are handed to the sheet when they point at an
            Item. A text entry, or a link to an actor or journal, is shown in the chat card but
            nothing is added.
        </p>
        <p class="field-hint">
            <strong>Every draw is independent.</strong> A table set to draw without replacement
            still repeats, because the roller never writes back to your table.
        </p>
    </div>

</div>
